atements is equivalent to the conjunction of the negations of the individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(2\\text{ is not prime}\\text{ or }2\\notin Q) & ≡¬((2\\text{ is not prime})∨(2\\notin Q)) \\\\  & ≡¬(2\\text{ is not prime})∧¬(2\\notin Q) \\\\  & ≡(2\\text{ is prime})∧(2\\in Q) \\\\  & ≡2\\text{ is prime}\\text{ and }2\\in Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401716 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401717 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401716 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401718 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401716 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401719 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401716 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401720 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401716 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401721 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401716 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401716 1077 "selection" 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401716 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401718 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401716 1080 #uuid "afaa16c5-b2b9-5a55-a11e-ac5052152f4f" 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401717 1081 "$2$ is not prime  or $2\\in Q$" 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401717 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401717 1084 #uuid "7e98d0ca-b7a2-5170-9381-24b76f0454f7" 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401718 1081 "$2$ is prime  and $2\\in Q$" 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401718 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401718 1084 #uuid "b8773b7b-5555-5c11-b984-7a58534070f3" 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401719 1081 "$2$ is not prime  and $2\\in Q$" 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401719 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533486 17592186045585 true] [17592186401719 1084 #uuid "e4a7643a-1d6b-53